WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.045
Wind has speed, direction, variation, and vertical structure.

00:00:04.045 --> 00:00:07.939
Average wind alone can hide gusts that briefly exceed a small drone's control margin.

00:00:07.939 --> 00:00:11.920
Compare forecast and observed conditions with manufacturer guidance, payload effects,

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.900
operator experience, and planned altitude.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.345
Structures and terrain disturb airflow.

00:00:16.345 --> 00:00:19.275
Buildings can create rotors, downwash, acceleration around corners,

00:00:19.275 --> 00:00:21.525
and turbulence on the downwind side.

00:00:21.525 --> 00:00:22.585
Trees, ridges, cliffs,

00:00:22.585 --> 00:00:26.365
and shorelines can produce localized movement that differs from an open-area reading.

00:00:26.365 --> 00:00:28.360
Plan the outbound and return legs together.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.895
A favorable tailwind leaving the site may become a strong headwind during return,

00:00:31.895 --> 00:00:33.649
increasing power use and time.

00:00:33.649 --> 00:00:37.250
Reserve battery for wind change, route adjustment, approach, and landing.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:40.250
Wind normally increases with height and can shift direction.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.625
Conditions at the launch point may not describe the mission altitude.

00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:46.090
Watch groundspeed, aircraft attitude, position-hold effort, power use,

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:49.200
and control response for signs that margins are narrowing.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.715
Payloads change wind sensitivity.

00:00:50.715 --> 00:00:52.870
A larger camera, guard, mapping attachment,

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:56.842
or unusual center of gravity can increase drag and reduce endurance.

00:00:56.842 --> 00:01:00.190
Manufacturer maximums are not operational targets; terrain, gusts,

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:02.815
and mission complexity justify additional margin.

00:01:02.815 --> 00:01:05.940
Use conservative go or no-go criteria and an early return point.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.635
If the aircraft struggles to hold position, battery use rises unexpectedly,

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:11.638
or turbulence degrades control or imagery,

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:14.200
end the mission before recovery becomes difficult.
